      "body": "## Membership organisations run on volunteer time\n\nYi Raipur — the Young Indians chapter we built WhatsOn for — has over three hundred members and an active calendar of events, philanthropy drives, climate and road-safety initiatives.\n\nThe people organising all of that are doing it alongside full-time jobs. Every hour spent chasing RSVPs in a WhatsApp group is an hour not spent on the work the community exists for.\n\n## Where the time actually goes\n\nCollecting RSVPs by counting thumbs-up reactions. Marking attendance on a printed sheet. Chasing a member list that is out of date the week after it is compiled. Assembling an activity report at year end from memory and photographs.\n\nNone of this is difficult. All of it is relentless.\n\n## What we build\n\nEvent listings with proper RSVPs. QR check-in that takes a second at the door and produces attendance data automatically. A member directory members maintain themselves. Offers and announcements that reach people without another WhatsApp group. Birthdays, because in a membership community those matter more than any feature list suggests.\n\n## Engagement becomes measurable\n\nOnce check-ins are digital, leadership can finally see which events draw people, which segments are drifting away, and what to do differently next year — with evidence instead of impressions.\n\n## Handover to volunteers\n\nThese platforms are inherited by whoever holds the role next year. We build accordingly: simple administration, written documentation, and no dependency on the one technical volunteer who set it up.",
